{"guid": "V05_042", "pos_type": "verb", "pos_subtype": "emotional_state", "concept_label": "enjoy (habitual liking)", "concept_definition": "To have a habitual liking for something or take pleasure in doing an activity regularly.", "translations": {"en": "enjoy", "lt": "mėgti", "zh": "喜欢", "fr": "aimer", "es": "disfrutar", "es-419": "disfrutar"}, "difficulty_level": 150, "disambiguation": {"lt": "general or habitual liking", "en": "habitual liking"}, "notes": "Lithuanian: mėgti expresses a general or habitual liking; Aš mėgstu skaityti — I enjoy reading. With a noun, use the accusative: Aš mėgstu kavą. Overlaps with patikti (like, L3), which uses a dative experiencer: Man patinka kava. The preference/reaction distinction is a tendency, not an absolute rule. Distinct teaching target from enjoy (take pleasure in an experience), mėgautis, L260."}
